We&nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&nbsp;and drive&nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.

Data Scientist, Marketing Effectiveness &amp; Testing &nbsp;

Are you a skilled data scientist seeking to contribute at a world-class company? Join Hasbro’s Marketing Efficiency &amp; Testing team in Renton, WA. Become part of a dynamic group dedicated to evaluating our marketing investments and customer initiatives. This role presents an outstanding chance to engage in high-impact projects across beloved Hasbro brands, including Magic: The Gathering, Dungeons &amp; Dragons, Monopoly, and emerging digital games. The position offers considerable ownership and autonomy for individuals who thrive in collaborative and innovative environments. &nbsp;

What You Will do as a Data Scientist: &nbsp;

• Develop and analyze marketing experiments and causal inference studies, including geo-holdouts, A/B tests, and synthetic controls &nbsp;

• Research and apply statistical, machine learning, and experimental methods to business problems &nbsp;

• Build forecasting models and analytical solutions for new and existing products, campaigns, and initiatives &nbsp;

• Integrate data from internal systems, third-party vendors, APIs, and external data providers &nbsp;

• Partner with Data Engineering teams to improve data availability and define requirements for new analytical capabilities &nbsp;

• Communicate findings and recommendations through clear visualizations, presentations, and documentation &nbsp;

• Support the development of Hasbro’s marketing data science initiatives &nbsp;

What You Will Bring: &nbsp;

• Proficiency&nbsp;with Python (Pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, visualization libraries), SQL, and git &nbsp;

• Statistical modeling and experimental design methods &nbsp;

• Experience working with large and complex datasets &nbsp;

• Proven ability to apply analytics, experimentation, and predictive modeling to solve business problems &nbsp;

• Experience crafting, analyzing, or interpreting experiments such as A/B tests, holdouts, geo-experiments, and other causal measurement frameworks &nbsp;

• Experience developing customer analytics such as segmentation, retention, acquisition, and lifetime value analyses &nbsp;

• Ability to work with marketing, customer, sales, and digital product data &nbsp;

• Strong communication&nbsp;skills to convey technical findings to non-technical audiences and business collaborators &nbsp;

• Familiarity with cloud-based analytics environments and modern data platforms&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Bachelor's degree in&nbsp;a quantitative&nbsp;field. &nbsp;

Nice to Have: &nbsp;

• Experience measuring marketing efficiency across digital and traditional media channels &nbsp;

• Experience with web analytics platforms such as Google Analytics, Adobe Analytics, or similar tools &nbsp;

• Familiarity with major advertising and marketing ecosystems including Amazon and Google &nbsp;

• Experience forecasting demand, sales, customer behavior, or business performance &nbsp;

• Experience with Databricks, Azure, Snowflake,&nbsp;dbt, or related analytics technologies &nbsp;

• Experience collaborating with Data Engineers or ML Engineers to operationalize analytical solutions &nbsp;

• Master’s degree or equivalent experience in statistics, economics, mathematics, computer science, physics, or another quantitative field &nbsp;

Compensation range, USD: &nbsp;

$102,500 - $153,700 &nbsp;

Join us at Hasbro and help build the future of our marketing strategies with your outstanding data science skills. Your work will directly contribute to the success of our iconic brands and delight mill

&nbsp;

This is a Full-Time Role (40 hours per week, 5DWW) with no option for part-time work. While this is a remote-first opportunity, the candidate filling this role must be a resident of the Netherlands, the U.K., Brazil, Pennsylvania, New York, or the District of Columbia at the start of employment. Additionally, they must be within commuting distance of our office in Amsterdam, London, São Paulo, Philadelphia, New York City, or Washington.&nbsp;
Please visit&nbsp; our Careers page to review all opportunities and submit your application for the role(s) that best fit your location and work authorization.

